      "summary": {
        "text": "Animated enhanced infrared (EIR) satellite imagery depicts a contracting eye, now measured at 31 NM, characterized by cooling eye temperatures (15C) and warming cloud-top temperatures within the central dense overcast (cdo). Typhoon (TY) 30W has begun its east- northeastward turn over the past six hours as the STR to the east shifts subtly southward and its northwestern boundary erodes in response to a mid-latitude shortwave trough passing to the north. Once the trough passes to the north in the next 6-12 hours, the STR to the west will strengthen and build eastward, while the ridge to the east weakens and shifts southward.",
